OL,3,CAll major Italian cities on red heat
OL,4,Calert as heatwave rips through Europe
OL,6,FTemperatures have climbed above 40C in
OL,7,Fseveral European countries, prompting
OL,8,Fhealth warnings for millions of people.
OL,10,FScientists and officials warn that
OL,11,Fextreme heat events are becoming more
OL,12,Ffrequent and intense as the climate
OL,13,Fwarms.
OL,15,FThe current heatwave has exposed
OL,16,Fvulnerabilities in public health
OL,17,Fsystems, power generation, transport
OL,18,Fnetworks, and tourism infrastructure,
OL,19,Fforcing governments and businesses to
OL,20,Fadapt to increasingly frequent periods
OL,21,Fof extreme weather.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
